  "summary": "A four-way directional control valve connects a pressure supply (P) and a return to tank (T) to two actuator ports (A and B). Shifting the spool reverses the connections — P→A with B→T, or P→B with A→T — so a double-acting cylinder extends and retracts. The same principle is used in pneumatic valves and in refrigeration reversing valves.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Directional control valve (hydraulic/pneumatic)",
    "type": "4/2 spool valve, double solenoid"
  },
